summary:
- topic: Student Recognition
  text: The SPHS Robotics Team 58, the Riot Crew, was recognized for their performance
    at the World Championships in Houston, where they ranked in the top 3%. The team
    demonstrated their robot for the board and received certificates of recognition.
- topic: FY24 Audit Report
  text: The board received a detailed report on the FY24 audit from the district's
    auditing firm, RKO. Key findings included material weaknesses in the reconciliation
    of grants and employee benefits, and a compliance finding for overspending. The
    district outlined corrective actions, including implementing monthly reconciliations,
    a budget freeze on non-essential spending, and continuing the search for a permanent
    finance director.
- topic: Personnel Actions and Recognition
  text: The board approved a lengthy list of second probationary and first continuing
    contracts. Additionally, the retirement of Craig Uffington, SPHS Band Director
    since 1994, was announced. Board members paid special tribute to his long and
    impactful career in music education.
- topic: Public Comment on Teacher Non-Renewals
  text: 'A significant portion of public comment was dedicated to advocating for the
    renewal of contracts for two educators: a pre-K special education teacher at Dyer
    Elementary and another special education teacher. Parents, colleagues, and the
    teachers themselves spoke about their dedication, skills, and the perceived lack
    of support and due process from the administration.'
- topic: South Portland High School Progress
  text: SPHS Principal Sarah Glenn presented an update on school progress, highlighting
    a 3% drop in chronic absenteeism, a significant decrease in out-of-school suspensions,
    and notable growth in average SAT scores, bringing the school more in line with
    the national average.
- topic: District Reorganization
  text: As part of a district reorganization, the board approved new job descriptions
    for a Human Resources Manager, an Assistant Principal of Teaching and Learning
    at SPHS, and a Dean of Students at SPHS.
- topic: School Board Vacancy
  text: The Chair announced a vacant seat on the school board, with interviews scheduled
    to be held by the City Council on May 13th.
- topic: Policy Updates
  text: The board approved a new job description policy for the superintendent. A
    second read and vote on an updated concussion policy was postponed to the next
    meeting to allow for clarification on parental approval for return-to-play protocols.
